  "notes": [
    "`T` read in seconds, from the step: the median step between rows is 0.05, and the reader reads one above 5 as milliseconds (at the manuals' 1 to 33 samples a second, a step is 0.03 to 1 in seconds and 30 to 1,000 in milliseconds)",
    "`Alt` read in feet, from the manual: the Classic's and TRS's manuals (p37) give the altitude in feet, the Quantum's and Proton's set every altitude in feet, and no Eggtimer manual offers another unit; the file's `AccelFPSS` is 32.19 times its `AccelG`, and one g is 32.17 ft/s²",
    "`Veloc` read in feet per second, from the altitude: it is the change in `Alt` over the step, within 1 % or 1 ft/s, in 39 of 39 rows after the first",
    "`VAccel` read in feet per second, from the manual: the Proton's manual (p45) gives the accelerometer's velocity in ft/sec",
    "`AltAccel` read in feet, from the manual: the Proton's manual (p45) gives the accelerometer's distance traveled in ft",
    "`FAlt` read in feet, from the manual: it is the logger's filtered `Alt` (Quantum p38, Proton p45), in the same unit",
    "`FVeloc` read in feet per second, from the altitude: it is the change in `FAlt` over the step, within 1 % or 1 ft/s, in 39 of 39 rows after the first",
    "`FAccelVel` read in feet per second, from the manual: the Proton's manual (p45) gives the accelerometer's velocity in ft/sec",
    "`FAccelAlt` read in feet, from the manual: the Proton's manual (p45) gives the accelerometer's distance traveled in ft",
    "5 rows hold only empty cells, and were skipped"
  ]
}
